{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cf9faB5yMCGPEL9RtMYnz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G79HYknBZafwHv1wzjLBhT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"ls .github/workflows/ && echo --- && cat .github/workflows/attavo-coherence.yml 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT FOUND\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1328,"cache_read_input_tokens":35717,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1328},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7cc9585-2355-4899-aa3b-79bd5e1f831b","uuid":"87da3e75-999e-461a-9908-816077dddd89","timestamp":"2026-09-17T20:46:02.602Z","request_id":"req_011Cf9faAaiC1myLxiGvzRk4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01G79HYknBZafwHv1wzjLBhT":{"command":"cd /Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-158 && ls .github/workflows/ && echo --- && cat .github/workflows/attavo-coherence.yml 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT FOUND\""}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01G79HYknBZafwHv1wzjLBhT":{"cwd":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-158"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G79HYknBZafwHv1wzjLBhT","type":"tool_result","content":"attavo-approve.yml\nattavo-coherence.yml\nattavo-spec-gate.yml\nci.yml\n---\n# Template. Copy this file into your own .github/workflows/ and fill in\n# uses: <owner>/attavo@<tag> below. Not vendored or executed by Attavo's\n# own repository -- this is the tenant's workflow, not the product's.\n#\n# `attavo attest` derives the merged item from the merge ref's own record\n# paths, refuses unless that item's chain holds, and prints the\n# attestation statement to stdout -- it never writes to the tree (issue\n# #69: the four stage records already under paths.records are the\n# evidence; this job seals them). This workflow runs it on pull_request,\n# against the pull request's own merge ref, and on merge_group, against\n# the exact tree the merge will produce, so an incoherent chain refuses\n# while the branch can still be pushed to.\n#\n# On pull_request the run line also carries --partial (issue #67): the\n# verify record a complete chain would need is the output of `attavo\n# verify`, which itself waits on this check going green, so the two\n# checks deadlock without it. --partial treats a missing later record as\n# \"not yet\" rather than a refusal, while still enforcing that a build's\n# approval_sha names the latest approval and a verify's build_sha names\n# the latest build. merge_group and a push to main still demand the whole\n# chain -- nothing runs after either that could still supply a record\n# found missing there. attest's stdout -- the statement, or a not-yet or\n# zero-item line -- is captured to a plain file, and the attest step\n# itself reads whether that file parses as a JSON object into its own\n# `statement` output: a python3 -c json.load check, its exit status read\n# into the output, never a grep -- a grep would say yes for any line that\n# merely looks like JSON, which a not-yet line's stage names could. The\n# not-yet and zero-item lines are prose, not JSON, and a merge group can\n# carry no item exactly as easily as a pull request can; without this\n# check the steps below would hand actions/attest that prose the moment\n# the pin lane's own installing merge -- which touches no item -- reached\n# the queue.\n#\n# Only on merge_group -- github.sha there resolves to the commit that\n# will actually land on main, not the merge queue's own temporary ref --\n# and only when attest's own output says the captured file is a\n# statement, two further steps run: a sha256 digest of that commit's own\n# sha text (deterministic and reproducible from the sha alone), and\n# actions/attest@v2, signing attest's printed statement as the predicate,\n# env.ATTAVO_ATTESTATION_PREDICATE_TYPE, over that digest. That variable\n# is action.yml's own export of the schema's $id, never typed here (issue\n# #117: v0.18.0 moved the $id from .../v1 to .../v2, and this template's\n# own copy of the literal did not move with it). Signing here replaces\n# the post-merge attest workflow this product shipped before (issue #69):\n# the four stage records are the evidence, and the bundle actions/attest@v2\n# writes to the forge's attestation store is the seal over them -- no\n# attestation record is ever written to the tree.\n#\n# Neither step carries continue-on-error. Ruled: a merge without a\n# signature is unattested, and the product's claim is that nothing merges\n# unattested, so a signing failure fails this required context and the\n# merge does not happen. This reverses the 2026-09-09 refusal-tolerance\n# ruling for the step that used to patch a record's signed field either\n# way; there is no record left for that patch to write to, and a tenant\n# whose signing provider is unavailable un-requires this context as its\n# own act, on its own ledger -- not a default this template supplies.\n#\n# This step is not folded into attavo-spec-gate.yml's job, for two\n# reasons: that job skips an ordinary pull request from any branch that\n# doesn't start with attavo/ (issue #12), and every step after its skip\n# step is skipped on a record-only commit. An approval push is a\n# record-only commit -- including a re-approval after a build, the exact\n# shape that broke the chain on tenant zero (approval-07, issue #62) --\n# so folding coherence into that job would skip the check on precisely\n# the commit most likely to need it. Coherence has neither restriction:\n# it runs on any pull request, record-only commit or not, and reports its\n# own required context so a tenant can gate the merge queue on it without\n# widening the spec-gate job's guards.\n#\n# actions/checkout@v4 takes no ref: -- the pull_request and merge_group\n# events default to the merge commit checkout already needs, the same\n# tree `attavo attest` reads git diff --name-only HEAD^1 HEAD against.\n# fetch-depth: 0 keeps that first parent reachable.\n#\n# No app token is minted and nothing is pushed: attest prints, it never\n# writes, and the signed statement lives in the forge's attestation\n# store, not in a commit this job makes.\nname: Attavo coherence\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]\n  merge_group:\n\njobs:\n  coherence:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      id-token: write\n      attestations: write\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n\n      - uses: attavo/attavo@v0.25.0\n\n      - name: attavo attest\n        id: attest\n        run: |\n          attavo attest ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && '--partial' || '' }} > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/attestation.json\"\n          if python3 -c \"import json,sys; sys.exit(0 if isinstance(json.load(open(sys.argv[1])), dict) else 1)\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/attestation.json\" 2>/dev/null; then\n            echo \"statement=true\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n          else\n            echo \"statement=false\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n          fi\n\n      - na