{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cf9gPyiCa6ZcUdvnG85DK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014M1t7FSf1TLE2JQ81vugHZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nattavo: proof five, every attested item is sealed (#158)\n\nThe doctor's fifth proof reads [forge].attestation_command for a merge\ncommit's statement in the forge's attestation store, so a chain that\nholds on its four stage records but was never sealed -- #106, #148,\n#153, merged direct with no merge_group run -- fails instead of\nreporting done. sealed_since names the commit before which this\ntenant's own merges predate the merge queue; they are reported as\nbefore the window rather than failed.\n\nforge-attestation re-derives the merge sha's synthetic subject digest\nand reads it back via `gh api`; the doctor checks sealed_since before\ncalling it, so a merge already known to predate the window costs no\nnetwork round trip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\ngit status --porcelain"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":534,"cache_read_input_tokens":66469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":534},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7cc9585-2355-4899-aa3b-79bd5e1f831b","uuid":"2b087644-8e94-41cc-9ad0-7119de70bb04","timestamp":"2026-09-17T20:56:54.611Z","request_id":"req_011Cf9gPyFAPBAneezzSbsvc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014M1t7FSf1TLE2JQ81vugHZ":{"command":"cd /Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-158 && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nattavo: proof five, every attested item is sealed (#158)\n\nThe doctor's fifth proof reads [forge].attestation_command for a merge\ncommit's statement in the forge's attestation store, so a chain that\nholds on its four stage records but was never sealed -- #106, #148,\n#153, merged direct with no merge_group run -- fails instead of\nreporting done. sealed_since names the commit before which this\ntenant's own merges predate the merge queue; they are reported as\nbefore the window rather than failed.\n\nforge-attestation re-derives the merge sha's synthetic subject digest\nand reads it back via `gh api`; the doctor checks sealed_since before\ncalling it, so a merge already known to predate the window costs no\nnetwork round trip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\ngit status --porcelain"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_014M1t7FSf1TLE2JQ81vugHZ":{"cwd":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-158"}}}
