{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cf9gQTz4AXp9TUs1q8YwA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed as `e45ed5e` on `attavo/158-sealed-proof`. I fixed one bug beyond the existing diff: `proof_every_attested_item_is_sealed` was calling the attestation command before checking `sealed_since`, which made every doctor run attempt a `gh api` network call for items that predate the merge queue (106, 148, 153) — that hung the test suite under this session's network sandbox. I reordered it to check `sealed_since` first, and updated `tests/test_record_schemas.py`'s `json.loads(` site count (5→6) since `statement_for` added a legitimate new non-record parse site. Full test suite passes except two pre-existing failures in `tests/test_adapters.py` unrelated to this issue's claims (adapter model-derivation logic, untouched by this change)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":548,"cache_read_input_tokens":67003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":548},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7cc9585-2355-4899-aa3b-79bd5e1f831b","uuid":"c8c70923-9842-4f4b-8291-8be19f7106ee","timestamp":"2026-09-17T20:56:59.465Z","request_id":"req_011Cf9gQTWXcZAR88ipo5nZx"}
